const groups=[
['qa','Quality Engineering',['Quality Assurance','Software Testing','Test Planning','Test Strategy','Regression Testing','Exploratory Testing','Acceptance Testing','Integration Testing','Unit Testing','Defect Tracking','Test Traceability','Test Reporting','Allure','Performance Testing','Security Testing','Accessibility Testing','Mobile Testing','Cross-Browser Testing','Authentication Testing'],'Start with a behavior, a risk, and observable evidence. Quality assurance prevents defects through requirements review, risk analysis, environments, data, and feedback; testing reveals information about the product. Write acceptance criteria before test cases, use risk to choose coverage, and link every requirement to tests and defects.','A test strategy defines why, what, where, and when to test. A test plan assigns people, data, environments, and reporting. Regression protects existing behavior; exploratory testing discovers unknown risk; acceptance testing proves business value. A high-quality defect report includes impact, reproducible steps, expected and actual behavior, build, data, screenshots, logs, and ownership.','Do not mistake a high pass rate for quality. Track defect escapes, flaky tests, risk coverage, execution time, and failure causes. Accessibility, performance, security, mobile, and browser compatibility are risk dimensions, not late-stage checkboxes.','Risk: duplicate payment\nDesign: test rapid click + API idempotency + final database balance\nEvidence: request ID, audit event, one transaction'],
['automation','Automation and Playwright',['Test Automation','Playwright','End-to-End Testing','Browser Automation','Network Interception','Visual Regression Testing','BDD','Cucumber','Page Object Model','Test Fixtures','Test Data Management'],'Use the test pyramid: many unit and API checks, fewer UI journeys. Automate repeatable, valuable checks with stable test data and clear ownership. Keep a small E2E suite for critical user flows.','Playwright uses isolated browser contexts, auto-waiting, semantic locators, traces, screenshots, and parallel workers. A Page Object Model centralizes interaction knowledge; fixtures provide authenticated state, API clients, and cleanup. BDD is useful when examples are a shared business language, not when it merely duplicates implementation detail.','Avoid fixed sleeps, brittle absolute XPath, shared accounts, and retries that turn failures into passes. Use network interception to simulate controlled boundaries, then keep contract or integrated coverage for the real dependency.','await page.getByRole("button", {name:"Pay"}).click();\nawait expect(page.getByText("Payment confirmed")).toBeVisible();'],
['engineering','Engineering Foundations',['JavaScript','TypeScript','Python','HTML','CSS','Responsive Web Design','Node.js','React','Express.js','FastAPI','Gradio','Pydantic'],'Model data explicitly and validate external input at the boundary. HTML supplies meaning, CSS presentation, and responsive design adapts layout. JavaScript provides runtime behavior; TypeScript catches type mismatches before runtime; Python is effective for automation, APIs, and data.','Use modules, small pure functions, explicit error handling, and dependency boundaries. React composes interface state; Node.js and Express expose JavaScript services; FastAPI and Pydantic provide typed Python APIs; Gradio is useful for fast ML interfaces.','Never trust a TypeScript assertion or an LLM/API payload without runtime validation. Prefer unknown plus a type guard, schema, or Pydantic model. Separate domain logic from HTTP, CLI, or UI adapters.','type Order={id:string;total:number};\nconst isOrder=(x:unknown):x is Order => typeof x==="object" && x!==null;'],
['api','APIs, Data, and Contracts',['REST APIs','API Testing','API Contract Testing','API Integration','Postman','JSON','JSON Schema','SQL','PostgreSQL','SQLite','MySQL','Redis','Webhooks','System Integration'],'HTTP status is only one signal. Validate the business result, schema, authorization, headers, idempotency, pagination, timeouts, and errors. GET reads, POST creates or triggers processing, PUT replaces, and PATCH changes a subset.','JSON is a representation; JSON Schema defines allowed shape. Contract tests prevent producers from silently breaking consumers. SQL queries relational data; PostgreSQL, MySQL, and SQLite differ operationally. Redis serves cache, queues, and ephemeral state rather than replacing durable records.','Treat webhooks as untrusted external events: verify signatures, acknowledge quickly, process idempotently, persist failures, and retry safely. Trace a discrepancy across database, API, cache, and UI with timestamps and request IDs.','const r=await request.get("/orders/o-1");\nexpect(r.status()).toBe(200);\nexpect(await r.json()).toMatchObject({id:"o-1"});'],
['delivery','Delivery and Infrastructure',['Git','GitHub','CI/CD','GitHub Actions','Jenkins','Docker','Docker Compose','Linux','DevOps','Cloud Deployment','Environment Variables','Secrets Management','Caddy','Reverse Proxy'],'Deliver small changes with a reviewed diff, a clear commit, automated verification, and a rollback path. Git records history; GitHub coordinates review; CI/CD runs repeatable checks and deployment.','Docker packages an application with dependencies. Docker Compose describes multi-service local systems. Linux operations require process, port, permission, log, and filesystem literacy. A reverse proxy such as Caddy terminates TLS and routes traffic.','Do not store secrets in source, browser bundles, logs, screenshots, or unprotected CI output. Configure with environment variables or a secret manager. A release gate should include risk tests, contracts, security, health signals, and ownership.','name: verify\non: [pull_request]\njobs: {test: {runs-on: ubuntu-latest, steps: [{run: "python scripts/verify.py"}]}}'],
['ai','AI Automation and Agents',['AI Automation','Workflow Automation','Automation','AI Agents','Large Language Models (LLMs)','Model Context Protocol (MCP)','MCP Server Development','n8n','LangGraph','LangChain','CrewAI','OpenAI API','Prompt Engineering','Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)','Agentic AI','AI Orchestration','Multi-Agent Systems','AI Evaluation','AI Safety','Human-in-the-Loop Systems','Structured Outputs','Tool Calling','Function Calling','LangSmith','Gemini','Groq','OpenRouter','YAML'],'An LLM predicts text; it does not grant permission, guarantee truth, or validate data. A good prompt states role, task, context, constraints, and output form. For consequential work, use structured output and validate it before invoking tools.','RAG retrieves source material before generation. Evaluate retrieval separately from answer quality. MCP standardizes discovery of tools, resources, and prompts; an MCP server should offer narrow, typed, least-privilege operations. LangChain, LangGraph, CrewAI, and n8n orchestrate different workflow styles.','Protect against prompt injection, over-broad tools, data leakage, infinite loops, and unbounded cost. Add approval for high-impact actions, log tool calls, cap retries/tokens, create evaluations, and make fallback behavior explicit.','{name:"create_ticket",parameters:{type:"object",required:["title"],properties:{title:{type:"string"}}}}'],
['operations','Reliability, Operations, and IoT',['Technical Operations','Observability','Logging','Alerting','Reliability Engineering','Incident Management','Operational Monitoring','Infrastructure Monitoring','Runbooks','Troubleshooting','Root Cause Analysis','System Administration','Self-Hosted Software','Internet of Things (IoT)','Home Assistant','MQTT','Sensors','Tuya','Hardware Integration','Home Automation','Automation Systems','Time-Series Data','Dashboard Design'],'Operate systems with logs, metrics, and traces. Logs explain events, metrics reveal trends, and traces connect work across services. Alerts must be actionable and tied to user impact.','Reliability engineering uses service indicators, objectives, error budgets, capacity planning, and safe change. During incidents: mitigate impact, communicate, preserve evidence, then conduct blameless root-cause analysis and track preventive actions in runbooks.','MQTT uses publish/subscribe topics for low-overhead IoT communication. Home Assistant, Tuya, sensors, and hardware integrations should have safe defaults, observability, and manual override. Store telemetry as time-series data and design dashboards for decisions, not decoration.','logger.info("payment_completed",{orderId,requestId,durationMs});'],
['data','Data and Professional Practice',['Data Quality','Data Validation','Data Pipelines','Data Processing','ETL','Data Analysis','Data Visualization','Data Documentation'],'Data quality means accuracy, completeness, consistency, timeliness, validity, and uniqueness. Validate inputs and outputs, define owners, and keep lineage.','ETL extracts, transforms, and loads; a reliable pipeline also needs schema checks, retries, observability, idempotency, and documentation. Analysis must state its assumptions; visualization must reveal rather than distort.','Document field meaning, source, refresh cadence, owner, privacy classification, and known limitations. Data contracts are the data equivalent of API contracts.','SELECT COUNT(*) AS missing_email FROM customers WHERE email IS NULL OR email = "";']
];
const toc=document.querySelector('#toc'),content=document.querySelector('#content');
groups.forEach(([id,title,skills,basics,practice,pitfalls,code],i)=>{toc.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<a href="#${id}">${i+1}. ${title}</a>`);content.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<section id="${id}"><p class="label">${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} / ${title.toUpperCase()}</p><h2>${title}</h2><h3>Fundamentals</h3><p>${basics}</p><h3>Practice and design</h3><p>${practice}</p><h3>Common mistakes and safeguards</h3><p>${pitfalls}</p><pre><code>${code.replaceAll('<','&lt;')}</code></pre><h3>Skills covered in this section</h3><div class="chips">${skills.join(' · ')}</div><p class="links">Related: <a href="#qa">quality strategy</a> · <a href="#api">contracts</a> · <a href="#delivery">delivery</a> · <a href="#operations">operations</a> · <a href="#ai">AI safety</a></p></section>`)});
